{
 "id": "page-breeding-bench-science",
 "target": "page",
 "page": "breeding-bench.html",
 "goal": "On the breeding bench: common bean's published minimum is 20 (self) and 10 plants is below it, sweet corn's is 100 (200 preferred), cross-pollinated by wind; 10 pollen and 90 seed parents give Ne = 4*10*90/100 = 36.0 and delta-F 1.39% (13.9% over 10 generations), 50/50 gives 100.0; sweet corn's cited isolation is two miles and 100 m is 3100 m short; keeping 10 of 100 is intensity 1.755 and an expected response 6.14 at h2 0.35 and SD 10, 50 of 100 is 0.798, 200 of 100 is refused; roguing 85 leaves 15 standing; the demo trial (4 entries x 3 blocks, means 10 12 11 14) has grand mean 11.75, MSE 0.167, LSD 0.82 kg, CV 3.5%; one replicate is not a trial; 90 of 100 seeds is 90.0% +/- 3.0% (84.1-95.9%), 30 of 20 is refused; 7 seasons stored is past the conventional window.",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "look",
   "action": "observe",
   "expect": {
    "ok": true,
    "snapshot.page": "breeding-bench.html"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pop",
